# Known divergences from the reference (metta-repl 0.2.10). Same format as tests/metta/.xfail:
#   <relative-path>  <STATUS>:<CATEGORY>:<id>  [notes]
# A test now passing is reported as UNEXPECTED_PASS — remove its line.

h02_atom_result_body.metta          ASSERT_FAIL:SEMANTIC_DIVERGENCE:atom-result-body   the body of an (-> … Atom) function is evaluated: (q3 (+ 1 2)) gives (foo 2 …)
h03_eval_one_step.metta             ASSERT_FAIL:SEMANTIC_DIVERGENCE:eval-one-step      eval reduces fully (42), the reference takes one step ((gg)); function/chain/return are not stepwise
h05_held_nondet.metta               ASSERT_FAIL:SEMANTIC_DIVERGENCE:force-first        __force takes the FIRST answer of a held non-deterministic term: (inc (superpose (1 2))) gives 2 only
h08_let_reduces_template.metta      ASSERT_FAIL:SEMANTIC_DIVERGENCE:let-rereduce       a let template is not reduced again after substitution: a built (+ 1 2) stays a term
h09_operator_as_body_data.metta     COMPILE_FAIL:KNOWN_BUG:op-as-body-data             (= (mk) (cons-atom + (1 2))) crashes the compiler: NotImplementedError it=+
h11_rules_for_compiled_head.metta   ASSERT_FAIL:FEATURE_PENDING:compiled-head-rules    a head compiled from the file ignores rules added/removed at run time (corpus selfprog)
